					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284#post-2106984</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-hub#post-2106984</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 10 Sep 2014 17:51:02 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Aelanna</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>334454</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p><em>artistic</em> is an attribute of SCP articles, hence why it's an adjective. I'm suggesting a new main tag such as <em>audio</em>, <em>video</em>, or <em>tale</em>, so <em>art</em> would work just fine. They would have distinct purposes and meanings.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284#post-2106895</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-hub#post-2106895</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 10 Sep 2014 16:04:15 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Tagliafierro</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1628788</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>As far as I know there is no &quot;art&quot; tag. There is an &quot;artistic&quot; tag, but no art. Maybe even &quot;drawing&quot; could work.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284#post-2106883</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-hub#post-2106883</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 10 Sep 2014 15:43:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Aelanna</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>334454</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>If that is the case, then it needs to be codified somewhere. It's going to be misleading and unfair to whatever poor newbie who comes along thinking it's okay to post art galleries, then gets slammed for not following procedure that doesn't exist anywhere except in staff's heads.</p> <p>Also, a new tag needs to be made for this. These aren't sandboxes; <em>sandbox</em> should refer to pages that are used for testing code and other things that require the context of the main site.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284#post-2105977</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-hub#post-2105977</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Sep 2014 15:11:58 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Fantem</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1391641</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Yeah, there was chat about that amongst staff. Don't quote me on it, but the general consensus was if:</p> <p><strong>A)</strong> the artist is a site member<br /> <strong>B)</strong> the artist has contributed a particularly substantial amount of high-quality art<br /> <strong>C)</strong> the art page they make survives the voting system</p> <p>then they'd get a setup like this.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
