					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284#post-2105964</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-hub#post-2105964</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Sep 2014 14:37:42 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Aelanna</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>334454</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>Arguably, there's also Kens's artwork page, the old personnel sketches file, and a good deal of pages with people's artwork (say, Rights's illustrated diary of old).</p> </blockquote> <p>I'm pretty sure all of these predate the move to the Visual Records Wiki, and thus avoided the unspoken rule that art that's not part of an article or tale needs to find a better place than the main site. If that is not the case, then it really needs to be put to paper. That's all I'm saying.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284#post-2105962</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-hub#post-2105962</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Sep 2014 14:34:34 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>VAElynx</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>914331</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>Also, and don't get me wrong because I think all of this work is fantastic, why do we have a single author who has special exemptions for posting artwork to the main wiki?</p> </blockquote> <p>Arguably, there's also Kens's artwork page, the old personnel sketches file, and a good deal of pages with people's artwork (say, Rights's illustrated diary of old).</p> <p>Which makes it less &quot;one time exception&quot; and more &quot;case-by-case decision&quot; which perhaps isn't a completely horrid thing, not the least because I'm unaware of many people actually wanting to have their art hosted here.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284#post-2105954</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-865284/sunnyclockwork-s-artwork-hub#post-2105954</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Sep 2014 14:25:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Aelanna</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>334454</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>Some images might not display, that means the link on the old page leads to an image that isn't there anymore or has errors.</p> </blockquote> <p>And that is why you don't hotlink to images served up by a CDN. Why was a special exemption to the hotlink rule made for this? Rules against hotlinking exist for reasons other than just permissions and bandwidth leeching (which I'm aware deviantArt allows hotlinking unless explicitly disallowed by the artist).</p> <p>Also, and don't get me wrong because I think all of this work is fantastic, why do we have a single author who has special exemptions for posting artwork to the main wiki? If this is to become a thing, then rules for posting artwork need to be actually laid down for the site rather than just, &quot;one person has special permission to do this, everyone else does not&quot;.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
